<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">jcb</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2064770</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">20070213820071008c</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1083/jcb.20070213820071008c</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>BubR1 and APC/EB1 cooperate to maintain metaphase chromosome alignment</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Jiayin</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Ahmad</surname><given-names>Sana</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>Yinghui</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>22</day><month>10</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><volume>179</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>357</lpage><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2007, The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2007</copyright-year><self-uri xlink:title="pdf" xlink:href="jcb1790357.pdf"/></article-meta></front><body><p>Vol. 178 No. 5, August 27, 2007. Pages <related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="178" page="773" id="N0x1c89250N0x3c0c4b0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="17709426" ext-link-type="pubmed">773&#x02013;784</related-article>.</p><p>After publication of this manuscript, the authors noticed that two images in Fig. 1 L were accidentally duplicated. Here we provide the corrected version of the <xref rid="fig1" ref-type="fig">figure</xref>. We apologize for this oversight.</p><fig position="float" id="fig1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>(L) Purification of recombinant <italic>Xenopus</italic> WT- and KD-BubR1. Initial <italic>E. coli</italic> lysates encoding GST&#x02013;WT-BubR1 (lane 1) and GST&#x02013;KD-BubR1 (lane 3) and GST&#x02013;WT-BubR1 (lane 2) and GST&#x02013;KD-BubR1 (lane 4) after affinity purification over immobilized glutathione.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcb1790357f01"></graphic></fig></body></article>